Subject: [PATCH 1/2] FsCache: invalidate the cache after a failed sector read

FsCache::prepare() reads the new sector directly into m_buffer. When
readSector() fails, it returns without updating m_sector, but the buffer
may already hold the new sector's bytes. The cache then reports the
previous sector as cached while holding different data. A later
prepare() or cacheSafeRead() for that sector returns the wrong bytes,
and a CACHE_FOR_WRITE prepare() writes them back to the card (to both
copies for a FAT sector).

With SHARED_SPI, SdSpiCard::readSectors() fills the whole buffer and
then sends CMD12. If CMD12 fails, readSector() returns false after the
buffer already holds the new sector.

Any dirty data is written back by sync() before the read starts, so
clearing the cache here does not lose data.

---
--- a/src/common/FsCache.cpp
+++ b/src/common/FsCache.cpp
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
     }
     if (!(option & CACHE_OPTION_NO_READ)) {
       if (!m_blockDev->readSector(sector, m_buffer)) {
+        // A failed transfer may have overwritten the old cached sector.
+        invalidate();
         DBG_FAIL_MACRO;
         goto fail;
       }
